{"id":"mahabharata-3-205","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":205,"title":"पञ्चाधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 205 · Kaushika told to serve his parents; the hunter's past","summary":{"en":"The hunter tells Kaushika that he has wronged his own parents by leaving them to study, and must return and serve them. Asked how he came to be born a hunter, he reveals that in a former life he was a Brahmin who wounded a sage by mistake while hunting and was cursed to be born a hunter.","kn":"ವೇದಾಧ್ಯಯನಕ್ಕಾಗಿ ತಂದೆತಾಯಿಯರನ್ನು ಬಿಟ್ಟು ಅವರಿಗೆ ಅನ್ಯಾಯ ಮಾಡಿರುವೆ, ಮರಳಿ ಅವರ ಸೇವೆ ಮಾಡು ಎಂದು ವ್ಯಾಧನು ಕೌಶಿಕನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ವ್ಯಾಧನಾಗಿ ಹೇಗೆ ಹುಟ್ಟಿದೆ ಎಂದು ಕೇಳಿದಾಗ, ಹಿಂದಿನ ಜನ್ಮದಲ್ಲಿ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣನಾಗಿದ್ದು ಬೇಟೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ತಪ್ಪಾಗಿ ಋಷಿಯನ್ನು ಗಾಯಗೊಳಿಸಿ ವ್ಯಾಧನಾಗಿ ಹುಟ್ಟೆಂದು ಶಾಪಗೊಂಡೆ ಎನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"व्याध कौशिक से कहता है कि अध्ययन के लिए माता-पिता को छोड़कर उन्होंने उनके साथ अन्याय किया है, और उन्हें लौटकर उनकी सेवा करनी चाहिए। यह पूछे जाने पर कि वह व्याध कैसे बना, वह बताता है कि पिछले जन्म में वह ब्राह्मण था जिसने शिकार में भूल से एक ऋषि को घायल कर दिया और व्याध होने का शाप पाया।","te":"చదువు కోసం తల్లిదండ్రులను విడిచి వారికి అన్యాయం చేశావని, తిరిగి వెళ్లి వారికి సేవ చేయమని వ్యాధుడు కౌశికునికి చెబుతాడు. వ్యాధుడిగా ఎలా పుట్టావని అడగగా, పూర్వజన్మలో బ్రాహ్మణుడిగా ఉండి వేటలో పొరపాటున ఒక ఋషిని గాయపరచి వ్యాధుడిగా పుట్టమని శాపం పొందానని వెల్లడిస్తాడు.","ta":"கல்விக்காகப் பெற்றோரை விட்டுச் சென்று அவர்களுக்குத் தீங்கிழைத்தீர், திரும்பி அவர்களுக்குப் பணிவிடை செய்யுங்கள் என்று வ்யாதன் கௌஶிகரிடம் சொல்கிறான். வேடனாக எப்படிப் பிறந்தாய் என்று கேட்க, முற்பிறவியில் அந்தணனாக இருந்து வேட்டையில் தவறுதலாக ஒரு முனிவரைக் காயப்படுத்தி வேடனாகப் பிறக்கச் சபிக்கப்பட்டதாக வெளிப்படுத்துகிறான்.","ml":"പഠിക്കാൻ പോയപ്പോൾ മാതാപിതാക്കളെ ഉപേക്ഷിച്ച് തെറ്റുചെയ്തുവെന്നും, മടങ്ങിച്ചെന്ന് അവരെ സേവിക്കണമെന്നും വ്യാധൻ കൗശികനോട് പറയുന്നു. താൻ എങ്ങനെ വ്യാധനായി ജനിച്ചുവെന്ന് ചോദിക്കുമ്പോൾ, പൂർവജന്മത്തിൽ വേട്ടയ്ക്കിടെ അബദ്ധത്തിൽ ഒരു മുനിയെ മുറിവേൽപ്പിച്ച ബ്രാഹ്മണനായിരുന്നുവെന്നും, അതിനാൽ വ്യാധനായി ജനിക്കാൻ ശപിക്കപ്പെട്ടുവെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം വെളിപ്പെടുത്തുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.205; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"मार्कण्डेयसमास्यापर्व","titleEn":"Markandeyasamasya Parva (Session with Markandeya)","verses":[{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"गुरू निवेद्य विप्राय तौ मातापितरावुभौ ।\nपुनरेव स धर्मात्मा व्याधो ब्राह्मणमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having handed his parents over to the brahmin as his teachers, the righteous hunter spoke to the brahmin once more."}},{"n":2,"text":"प्रवृत्तचक्षुर्जातोऽस्मि संपश्य तपसो बलम् ।\nयदर्थमुक्तोऽसि तया गच्छस्व मिथिलामिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"My eyes are opened now; see the power of austerity. She told you to go to Mithila for this very reason.\""}},{"n":3,"text":"पतिशुश्रूषपरया दान्तया सत्यशीलया ।\nमिथिलायां वसन्व्याधः स ते धर्मान्प्रवक्ष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"In Mithila lives a hunter devoted to serving her husband, self-controlled and true to her word, and he will teach you the dharmas.\" (The brahmin had been sent by a faithful wife.)"}},{"text":"ब्राह्मण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The brahmin said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"पतिव्रतायाः सत्यायाः शीलाढ्याया यतव्रत ।\nसंस्मृत्य वाक्यं धर्मज्ञ गुणवानसि मे मतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Remembering the words of that devoted, truthful and virtuous wife, O knower of dharma of firm vows, I judge you to be a man of real merit.\""}},{"text":"व्याध उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The hunter said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"यत्तदा त्वं द्विजश्रेष्ठ तयोक्तो मां प्रति प्रभो ।\nदृष्टमेतत्तया सम्यगेकपत्न्या न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"What she told you about me then, O best of brahmins, she saw rightly, being a devoted wife; there is no doubt of it.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"त्वदनुग्रहबुद्ध्या तु विप्रैतद्दर्शितं मया ।\nवाक्यं च शृणु मे तात यत्ते वक्ष्ये हितं द्विज ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I showed you all this out of a wish to do you good. Now hear the advice I give for your benefit.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"त्वया विनिकृता माता पिता च द्विजसत्तम ।\nअनिसृष्टोऽसि निष्क्रान्तो गृहात्ताभ्यामनिन्दित ।\nवेदोच्चारणकार्यार्थमयुक्तं तत्त्वया कृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You left your mother and father without their leave, blameless one, and went out of the house for the sake of reciting the Vedas. That was not a proper thing to do.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"तव शोकेन वृद्धौ तावन्धौ जातौ तपस्विनौ ।\nतौ प्रसादयितुं गच्छ मा त्वा धर्मोऽत्यगान्महान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Grieving for you, those two ascetics have grown old and blind. Go and appease them, so that great dharma does not pass you by.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"तपस्वी त्वं महात्मा च धर्मे च निरतः सदा ।\nसर्वमेतदपार्थं ते क्षिप्रं तौ संप्रसादय ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You are an ascetic, a great soul, always devoted to dharma, yet all of this is wasted for you. Go quickly and win them back.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"श्रद्दधस्व मम ब्रह्मन्नान्यथा कर्तुमर्हसि ।\nगम्यतामद्य विप्रर्षे श्रेयस्ते कथयाम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Trust me, brahmin; do not act otherwise. Go today, sage; I am telling you what is best for you.\""}},{"text":"ब्राह्मण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The brahmin said:"}},{"n":11,"text":"यदेतदुक्तं भवता सर्वं सत्यमसंशयम् ।\nप्रीतोऽस्मि तव धर्मज्ञ साध्वाचार गुणान्वित ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Everything you have said is true without doubt. I am pleased with you, knower of dharma, man of good conduct and virtue.\""}},{"text":"व्याध उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The hunter said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"दैवतप्रतिमो हि त्वं यस्त्वं धर्ममनुव्रतः ।\nपुराणं शाश्वतं दिव्यं दुष्प्रापमकृतात्मभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You are like a god, since you follow that ancient, eternal, divine dharma which is hard for the unrefined to reach.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"अतन्द्रितः कुरु क्षिप्रं मातापित्रोर्हि पूजनम् ।\nअतः परमहं धर्मं नान्यं पश्यामि कंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Without laziness, quickly serve your mother and father. I see no other dharma higher than this.\""}},{"text":"ब्राह्मण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The brahmin said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"इहाहमागतो दिष्ट्या दिष्ट्या मे संगतं त्वया ।\nईदृशा दुर्लभा लोके नरा धर्मप्रदर्शकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"By good fortune I came here, and by good fortune I met you. Men who show others dharma are rare in the world.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"एको नरसहस्रेषु धर्मविद्विद्यते न वा ।\nप्रीतोऽस्मि तव सत्येन भद्रं ते पुरुषोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Among thousands of men there may be one who knows dharma, or none. I am pleased with your truthfulness; may good come to you, best of men.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"पतमानो हि नरके भवतास्मि समुद्धृतः ।\nभवितव्यमथैवं च यद्दृष्टोऽसि मयानघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You have lifted me up as I was falling into hell. So it was fated that I should meet you, blameless one.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"राजा ययातिर्दौहित्रैः पतितस्तारितो यथा ।\nसद्भिः पुरुषशार्दूल तथाहं भवता त्विह ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"As King Yayati, fallen, was rescued by his daughters' sons, good men, tiger among men, so have you rescued me here.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"मातापितृभ्यां शुश्रूषां करिष्ये वचनात्तव ।\nनाकृतात्मा वेदयति धर्माधर्मविनिश्चयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"At your word I will serve my mother and father. One of unrefined mind cannot tell right from wrong.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"दुर्ज्ञेयः शाश्वतो धर्मः शूद्रयोनौ हि वर्तता ।\nन त्वां शूद्रमहं मन्ये भवितव्यं हि कारणम् ।\nयेन कर्मविपाकेन प्राप्तेयं शूद्रता त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Eternal dharma is hard to know, yet you live in a shudra birth. I do not think you a shudra; there must be a cause, some ripening of past deeds that brought you to this state.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"एतदिच्छामि विज्ञातुं तत्त्वेन हि महामते ।\nकामया ब्रूहि मे तथ्यं सर्वं त्वं प्रयतात्मवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I wish to know this truly, great-minded one. Out of kindness tell me the whole truth, with a settled mind.\""}},{"text":"व्याध उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The hunter said:"}},{"n":21,"text":"अनतिक्रमणीया हि ब्राह्मणा वै द्विजोत्तम ।\nशृणु सर्वमिदं वृत्तं पूर्वदेहे ममानघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Brahmins, best of the twice-born, must never be slighted. Hear the whole account of my previous body, blameless one.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"अहं हि ब्राह्मणः पूर्वमासं द्विजवरात्मज ।\nवेदाध्यायी सुकुशलो वेदाङ्गानां च पारगः ।\nआत्मदोषकृतैर्ब्रह्मन्नवस्थां प्राप्तवानिमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"In an earlier life I was a brahmin, the son of a brahmin of high rank, a student of the Veda, very skilled and master of the Vedic limbs. By faults of my own I came to this condition.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"कश्चिद्राजा मम सखा धनुर्वेदपरायणः ।\nसंसर्गाद्धनुषि श्रेष्ठस्ततोऽहमभवं द्विज ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"A certain king, devoted to archery, was my friend. Through his company I became expert with the bow, O brahmin.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"एतस्मिन्नेव काले तु मृगयां निर्गतो नृपः ।\nसहितो योधमुख्यैश्च मन्त्रिभिश्च सुसंवृतः ।\nततोऽभ्यहन्मृगांस्तत्र सुबहूनाश्रमं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"At that time the king went out hunting, accompanied by his chief warriors and surrounded by ministers, and he killed very many deer near a hermitage.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"अथ क्षिप्तः शरो घोरो मयापि द्विजसत्तम ।\nताडितश्च मुनिस्तेन शरेणानतपर्वणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then I too let fly a terrible arrow, best of brahmins, and it struck a sage with its smooth-jointed shaft.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"भूमौ निपतितो ब्रह्मन्नुवाच प्रतिनादयन् ।\nनापराध्याम्यहं किंचित्केन पापमिदं कृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Fallen to the ground, brahmin, he cried out: 'I have done no wrong to anyone. Who has done this sinful deed?'\""}},{"n":27,"text":"मन्वानस्तं मृगं चाहं संप्राप्तः सहसा मुनिम् ।\nअपश्यं तमृषिं विद्धं शरेणानतपर्वणा ।\nतमुग्रतपसं विप्रं निष्टनन्तं महीतले ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Thinking I had hit a deer, I rushed up suddenly. Then I saw the sage pierced by the arrow, that fiercely ascetic brahmin groaning on the ground.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"अकार्यकरणाच्चापि भृशं मे व्यथितं मनः ।\nअजानता कृतमिदं मयेत्यथ तमब्रुवम् ।\nक्षन्तुमर्हसि मे ब्रह्मन्निति चोक्तो मया मुनिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"My mind was deeply pained at having done what should not be done. I said to him, 'I did this without knowing; please forgive me, brahmin.'\""}},{"n":29,"text":"ततः प्रत्यब्रवीद्वाक्यमृषिर्मां क्रोधमूर्छितः ।\nव्याधस्त्वं भविता क्रूर शूद्रयोनाविति द्विज ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then the sage, faint with anger, answered me: 'Cruel man, you shall be born a hunter, in a shudra womb.'\""}}]}]}